# Discovery when the first greeting is lost (docs/pageflip.md section 4.2). Both halves run this
# script; which one is left and which is right comes from the settings file, as on a device.
#
# The harness makes each instance drop the first datagram it sends, which is its greeting. On
# loopback nothing is ever lost, so this case cannot happen here unless it is asked for -- and on a
# real radio it is ordinary. Two devices switched on together produce it without any loss at all:
# each greets while the other's radio is still coming up.
#
# Nothing is pressed. The only question is whether the pair forms at all.
log pageflip-discovery: start
expect_timeout 60000
expect Entering activity: Home
wait 800
tap confirm
expect Entering activity: EpubReader
expect peer present
wait 2000
log pageflip-discovery: done
quit
